      "evidence" : [
        {
          "detail" : "X table moves in world −X; Y carriage carries Z head. Component inheritance and mapped home positions are checked. Selected Z and upper-Y CAD contacts corroborate the authored bounds; this is not an exhaustive travel\/collision check.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "fusion-definition",
            "geometry-tests"
          ],
          "status" : "source",
          "topic" : "kinematics"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "q=(MPosX,MPosY+69,MPosZ+79.9) matches the supplied controller and CAD home anchors. Its algebra is validated digitally; physical switch trip, pull-off and datum offsets remain to be measured.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "shared-readme",
            "fusion-definition"
          ],
          "status" : "inferred",
          "topic" : "controllerMapping"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "CAD only: OpenCascade converts source centimetres to millimetres. All 52 exported solids agree with the inspected Fusion body bounds to within 0.000003 mm.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "step-audit",
            "geometry-tests"
          ],
          "status" : "measured",
          "topic" : "modelGeometry"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "The complete read-only export restores all nine Cover bodies. All 52 authored bodies are mapped, including the enclosure and chip guards. The simplified source still omits some hardware; full machining collision clearance is not certified.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "step-audit",
            "fusion-audit"
          ],
          "status" : "verified",
          "topic" : "geometryCoverage"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "The physical seating frame is separate from machining axes. Local X follows the slots, local Z points away from the table. A 203.2 × 37 × 50.8 mm reference block sits on the measured CAD support plane with 0.000137 mm maximum error and fits its footprint. The historical Fusion setup issue is not claimed to have been reproduced.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "geometry-tests",
            "geometry-resolution"
          ],
          "status" : "verified",
          "topic" : "stockPlacement"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "The table defines slot geometry, while each fixture defines its fasteners. The Bookend's custom M5 nut and key have zero CAD overlap in both slots. This is seated geometric fit, not thread strength, insertion-path or installed-hardware validation.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "geometry-tests",
            "geometry-resolution"
          ],
          "status" : "measured",
          "topic" : "mountingInterfaces"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "Manufacturer manual usable range 1500–8000 RPM is applied to generated programs. Firmware parameters 1360–8500 RPM describe a different limit and remain in the original source.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "controller-review",
            "fusion-definition"
          ],
          "status" : "source",
          "topic" : "usableSpindle"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "Pinned manufacturer firmware corroborates supplied travel, rates and reported spindle parameters. Installed controller settings have not been read.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "controller-review",
            "shared-readme"
          ],
          "status" : "source",
          "topic" : "controllerDefaults"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "150 W remains the existing Coastline planning estimate, not a manufacturer rating or measured cutting power.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "package-policy"
          ],
          "status" : "inferred",
          "topic" : "spindlePower"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "ER11 8 mm shank acceptance and nominal 22.9 mm seating depth have distinct manufacturer references. The supplied 75 mm overall-length cap replaces the unsubstantiated legacy 76.2 mm cap. The imported 7 mm tool-diameter limit is preserved as source metadata; actual tool stickout remains a per-setup measurement.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "controller-review",
            "fusion-definition"
          ],
          "status" : "source",
          "topic" : "toolLimits"
        },
        {
          "detail" : "Coastline explicitly selects coastline.grbl.desktop.v1. Generated text and local preflight regressions cover feed\/arc modes, usable RPM, bounded comments and manual tooling. system:\/\/grbl.cps is preserved as Fusion provenance, not executed. No machine command was sent.",
          "sourceIDs" : [
            "controller-review"
          ],
          "status" : "verified",
          "topic" : "nativePost"
        }
      ],
